Hi Ben,

Thanks for the question.  In the model language, the for loop must be over sequential integers given using a colon.  The more general "for(yr in bigYears)" is not supported for the model language.  I think you could do it like this:

for(yr in 1:num_bigYears){
PopVector[1:nmass, bigYears[yr]] <- getWintVec(zrv[1:nmass],zsv[1:nmass],Gw=Gw[1:nmass,1:nmass],popVec=PopVector[1:nmass,bigYears[yr]-1],1.99243,s.slp=sSlope,strv=starv[1:nmass])
    PopVector[1:nmass, bigYears[yr]+1] <- getSumrVec(zr.v=zrv[1:nmass],zs.v=zsv[1:nmass],Gs=Gs[1:nmass,1:nmass],Ds=Ds[1:nmass,1:nmass],popVec=PopVector[1:nmass,bigYears[yr]],s.int <http://s.int/>=1.99243,s.slp=sSlope,strv=starv[1:nmass],sJuv=0.6,warble[1:nmass],ost[1:nmass])
 <etc...>
}

where num_bigYears is a constant set to length(bigYears).

Does it make sense?

Perry

