That's curious indeed about the seeds.  Sometimes in models with discrete layers of parameters, some initialization at a higher level can lead to impossible situations in lower levels, thus the warning you're seeing.  So my guess is that for some seeds, the automatic-initialization at the higher levels leads to impossible initialization at the lower levels, and that warnings.  But again, it would require looking carefully at your code.  For now, I would just suggest initializing all variables in the model.

